Rust MLS surface preparation and sparse graph construction follow the DimOS MLS
shape, adapted for LingTu's native OctoMap and robot geometry.

Reference implementation:
https://github.com/dimensionalOS/dimos/blob/26144f7fd8424bdc33ab97dcd58e9497f2d413ee/dimos/navigation/global_planner/mls_planner/rust/src/surfaces.rs

The production planner now uses `src/kernels/nav/mls_core` for observed and
inferred surfaces, nodes, edges, and prepared-cache restore. OctoMap remains
the source for raw occupancy and final body/swept geometry checks. The C++
SurfaceIndex implementation is no longer part of the OctoPlanner build.

DimOS-derived code is covered by the Apache 2.0 terms in LICENSE-Apache-2.0.
The vendored OctoPlanner source remains under its accompanying MIT LICENSE.
